        <mxCell id="2PO_8HNQe2ZYQ-Khn99--86" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;Notes:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;ol style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;Negative Pack Isolation Relay #2 may be required, depending on application and local codes&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;Precharge Relay is required/strongly suggesteed for inverter type appications&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;Resistor sizing depends on Capacitor bank but 25-50watt 10-50 ohms is typical.&amp;nbsp; See manual for more detail&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;48V system power is shown as coming from bank #1 but if a DC/DC stepdown converter is available for your total system voltage it is the preferred solution.&amp;nbsp; See &quot;Converter Wiring&quot; page for example&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;Relay #1 is used as a pre-discconnect charger disable.&amp;nbsp; Check to see if your inerter has a &quot;remote charge disable&quot; input&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;DC power fusing is not shown but is required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;These dwgs are for example purposes only and do not supercede local codes, manufacturers manuals or good engineering practices&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;Video Links:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; Network Wiring explained:&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://youtu.be/u5sDKXkEIbQ&quot;&gt;https://youtu.be/u5sDKXkEIbQ&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; Wifi Setup and connecting:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://youtu.be/yG7mZW60KHo&quot; style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;https://youtu.be/yG7mZW60KHo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 9px;&quot;&gt;Editable Version of this file:&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://rec-bms-na.com/diagrams-net-rec-bms-libraries/&quot;&gt;https://rec-bms-na.com/diagrams-net-rec-bms-libraries/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;strokeColor=none;align=left;fillColor=none;html=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=10;" parent="2PO_8HNQe2ZYQ-Khn99--12" vertex="1">
